{"id":"6da70a87682c611a","group":"58","path":"58/batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md","title":"Self-Adjoint Operator","display":"df-self-adjoint-operator — Self-Adjoint Operator","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-self-adjoint-operator","aliases":["58-df-self-adjoint-operator","Self-Adjoint Operator"],"display":"df-self-adjoint-operator — Self-Adjoint Operator","depends_on":["[[../batch12/58-df-adjoint.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-self-adjoint-operator"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-self-adjoint-operator</span><span>Self-Adjoint Operator</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-self-adjoint-operator — Self-Adjoint Operator"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"200eacd293b1282b\" href=\"?note=200eacd293b1282b\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-adjoint.md\">../batch12/58-df-adjoint.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T,\\mathcal H,T^*\\in V\">\\(T,\\mathcal H,T^*\\in V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S\\subseteq V^4\">\\(\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S\\subseteq V^4\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"200eacd293b1282b\" href=\"?note=200eacd293b1282b\" title=\"../batch12/58-df-adjoint.md\">../batch12/58-df-adjoint.md</a>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S\\subseteq V^2\">\\(\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S\\subseteq V^2\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}self\\text{-}adjoint\\text{-}operator} \\vdash\n\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(T,\\mathcal H)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists T^*\\in V\\;(\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S(T,T^*,\\mathcal H,\\mathcal H)\\land T=T^*)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}self\\text{-}adjoint\\text{-}operator} \\vdash\n\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(T,\\mathcal H)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists T^*\\in V\\;(\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S(T,T^*,\\mathcal H,\\mathcal H)\\land T=T^*)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Self-adjoint: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T = T^*\">\\(T = T^*\\)</span>; crucial for quantum mechanics; ensures unitary time evolution</li>\n<li>Essential self-adjointness is an unbounded-operator notion requiring graph closure and is not defined through the bounded-adjoint predicate used here.</li>\n<li>Spectrum: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sigma(T) \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}\">\\(\\sigma(T) \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}\\)</span>; no imaginary spectrum possible</li>\n<li>Spectral theorem: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T = \\int_\\mathbb{R} \\lambda dE(\\lambda)\">\\(T = \\int_\\mathbb{R} \\lambda dE(\\lambda)\\)</span> with PVM <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"E\">\\(E\\)</span>; functional calculus</li>\n<li>Kato: self-adjoint perturbation theory; stability under bounded perturbations</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reed and Simon, Functional Analysis</li>\n<li>Simon, Modern Mathematical Physics</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch12/58-df-adjoint.md","status":"resolved","id":"200eacd293b1282b","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch12/58-df-adjoint.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch12/58-df-adjoint.md","status":"resolved","id":"200eacd293b1282b","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S\\subseteq V^4$ (see [[../batch12/58-df-adjoint.md]]).","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"T,\\mathcal H,T^*\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S\\subseteq V^4","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S\\subseteq V^2","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}self\\text{-}adjoint\\text{-}operator} \\vdash\n\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S(T,\\mathcal H)\\leftrightarrow\n\\exists T^*\\in V\\;(\\mathrm{Adjoint}_S(T,T^*,\\mathcal H,\\mathcal H)\\land T=T^*)","display":true},{"tex":"T = T^*","display":false},{"tex":"\\sigma(T) \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}","display":false},{"tex":"T = \\int_\\mathbb{R} \\lambda dE(\\lambda)","display":false},{"tex":"E","display":false}],"bytes":1320,"backlinks":[{"id":"c0bb7c1368e3c7b0","anchor":"ref-2","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S:V^2\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ (see [[../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md]])"},{"id":"a07bf08781c5a82a","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\operatorname{SelfAdjoint}_S$ (self-adjoint predicate, see [[../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md]])"},{"id":"340d68d16ad589e7","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"a11585cba9c21cfd","anchor":"ref-353","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[58-df-self-adjoint-operator]]"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-1126","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch14/58-df-self-adjoint-operator.md|58-df-self-adjoint-operator]]（batch14）"}],"outgoing":["200eacd293b1282b"]}